k  ordered product and that means people  are more than willing to fork over 19  as long as there's an apple logo on it  which brings us to our next point the  pricing sweet spot  analysts i spoke to said that apple's  fascination with the number 19 shows  that the company believes 19 is neither  too high nor too low but just right to  woo prospective buyers  if apple were to sell products far below  20  it might make the brand appear cheap and  that would not align with the premium  market that apple wants to dominate  and the price point could also speak to  the type of customer that apple wants to  attract if they wanted everybody as  their customer i think that they would  be pricing different products slightly  lower that's gene munster a tech stock  analyst who has covered apple for over a  decade for example you might not buy  this adapter by itself but it's easy to  add on and toss it in the cart when  you're buying something more expensive  say i'm on the market for a new macbook  this one has apple's new m1 pro chip and  if i add it to my cart for say  1999 dollars what's another 19 on top of  that i might even add two 19 items for  good measure apple's products are  generally more expensive than your  average devices and they tend to attract  shoppers who are willing to pay more  especially since with apple consumers  seem to think they already know what  they're going to get what matters is  that they're getting something from a  brand that they trust  and ultimately apple has consumers that  are willing to  make that jump even though as a  percentage it's  certainly expensive but this concept of  i'm an apple user and i want to surround  myself with all apple products that have  that seal of approval when i reached out  for thoughts from apple a spokesman  declined to comment apple says it prices  its offerings to be competitive but  let's be clear there are cheaper  alternatives out there too  not every company charges nineteen  dollars for very simple products  in fact  most of these nineteen dollar items can  be found somewhere else for much cheaper  so here's apple's cloth the 19 rag that  someone let me borrow because i couldn't  get my hands on it myself as you can see  the wait time is at least 10 weeks  but now that i have it it's soft it  looks nice almost has a suede-like  texture and it even gets fingerprints  off my computer  i tried to find a similar one on amazon  so i read through some reviews and after  about two days i got these a pack of  three for about nine bucks  they work just fine  they look nice too and they got  fingerprints off my gadgets and i have a  couple to spare them in case i lose one  so what does this all mean for you a few  things one if you don't care about brand  loyalty or don't care about little apple  stickers with your purchase you can buy  just as good products from other  retailers that will work just fine on  your apple gadgets and next time you  want to purchase a 19 charging adapter  remember that apple used to include that  in the box with iphones at no additional  charge  analysts told me that going with  products from other brands particularly  those on the lower end might have you  wishing you had just paid the premium a  polishing cloth probably isn't that  thing though what do you make of apple's  pricing psychology have you noticed any  of it at all  comment below and let me know your  thoughts and if you want to watch more  apple related content check out this  video on their new privacy policy also  be sure to subscribe to stay up to date  on the latest gadgets and the industry  that's powering them

